# Svelte component conventions

## Svelte 5 runes (required)

- Use `$props()` for component input — no `export let`
- Use `$derived()` for computed values
- Use `{@render children()}` for default slot content; typed as `Snippet` when using TypeScript
- Runes mode is forced project-wide in `svelte.config.js`

## Where components live

```
src/lib/components/
  layout/       PageContent, PageHeader, PageShell, PageMeta, SiteChrome, SiteHeader, SiteFooter, ErrorPage, ThemeToggle
  typography/   Text, Heading, Link
  primitives/   Button, Surface
  media/        Image
  content/      ParagraphArray, DesignGuideBody, DesignGuideFigure, DesignGuideToc
  sections/     MediaArticleSection, FaqSection, HeroSection, FeatureCarousel, SalesIntroSection, ContactCtaSection
  data/         DescriptionList
```

- **No `Typography.svelte`** — typography is `Text` + `Heading` + `Link` only
- **Images:** use `Image` from `media/Image.svelte` with required `src`, `alt`, `width`, `height` (optional `caption`, `priority`, `sizes`, `srcset`). Content image shape is `ContentImage` in `src/lib/content/types.ts`
- **Panels/cards** — use `Surface`, not new one-off card components
- **Capabilities / key-value rows** — use `DescriptionList`, not HTML tables for non-tabular data

- New shared UI goes here — not inline in route pages
- Page files in `src/routes/` should stay thin: compose components, set metadata via `PageMeta`

## Shared components

Prefer typography components (`Text`, `Heading`, `Link`); global heading classes remain valid. Shared UI inventory matches the folder map above.

## Props pattern

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
	import type { Snippet } from 'svelte';

	interface Props {
		children: Snippet;
	}

	let { children }: Props = $props();
</script>
```

- Require `lang="ts"` for components and route pages
- Prefer `PageData` / `LayoutData` from `./$types` on routes

## Composition

- Pass copy via props or snippets — do not hardcode user-facing text in components
- Page content comes from `data.content` (assembled in `src/lib/content/site.ts` from `src/lib/content/pages/*.ts`, loaded in `(site)/[[lang=locale]]/+layout.ts`)
- In-site links: `hrefFor(pageKey, locale)` from `src/lib/routes.ts` — never hardcode slugs
- Use `PageShell` for page padding + `.container` (one page width; no `narrow`/`wide`); use `PageContent` for readable body width (`.text-width`); use `Surface` for card/panel backgrounds
- Use `Text` with `variant` (`body` | `lead` | `caption` | `label`) instead of ad-hoc font sizes

## Component extraction rule of thumb

Ask: is this used (or will be used) on 2+ pages?

1. **2+ pages (or 2+ times on home)?** → `sections/` or `layout/`
2. **Style-only, no layout?** → `typography/` or `primitives/`
3. **Renders content arrays?** → `content/`
4. **Used once?** → keep in the page for now

New section components go in `sections/`. Name by purpose (`HeroSection`, `FeatureGrid`), not by page.

Do not add categories (atoms/molecules) or generic wrappers (`Grid`, `Stack`) — CSS variables and `PageContent` are enough for this site.

## Do not

- Introduce Svelte 4 patterns (`export let`, `$$props`, slots without snippets)
- Add component-scoped styles that duplicate tokens already in `app.css`
- Create one-off components for content that belongs in `src/lib/content/`
- Define URL slugs outside `src/lib/routes.ts`
- Add `Typography.svelte` or duplicate typography abstractions
- Add new `.js` modules under `src/` — use TypeScript
